UPDATE companies SET description='Race Tech Race Cars and Components, Inc. was founded in 1988 in Burlington, North Carolina, by champion driver and builder Russ Farmer, who remains president and CEO. The company began as a specialist builder of custom race cars and has grown into a full-service operation for drag racing competitors.

The shop produces custom-built dragsters, roadsters, and doorslammers, each designed in CAD to individual specifications. In-house capabilities include chassis and body fabrication, MIG/TIG welding, tube bending, CNC plasma cutting on a 4-by-8-foot table, and finishing services such as powder coating, polishing, chroming, and custom painting. The company also assembles AN braided stainless hoses as an authorized Goodridge distributor and offers nitrous bottle refills.

Race Tech serves drag racing teams across the NHRA Sportsman ranks and bracket-racing enthusiasts.

The company emphasizes reliability and ease of maintenance, citing design features such as removable crossmembers for transmission access, master cylinders mounted outside the driver compartment, and optimized driveline angles. Farmer notes that the parts division aims to match or beat warehouse pricing while providing technical expertise.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Body fabrication", "Chassis fabrication", "Custom fabrication", "AN hose assembly", "CNC plasma cutting", "Aluminum fabrication", "Sheet metal fabrication", "CAD design", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Tube bending", "Powder coating", "Polishing", "Chroming", "Custom painting", "Graphics application", "Nitrous bottle refilling"], "industries": ["Drag racing", "Bracket racing", "NHRA Sportsman"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Steel", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["4''x8'' CNC plasma table"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom CAD-designed race cars built to individual specifications", "In-house powder coating, polishing, chroming, and custom painting", "CNC plasma cutting of aluminum, steel, and stainless up to 1/4 inch", "AN hose assembly with Goodridge fittings, sizes -3 to -16", "Nitrous bottle refills on site"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 -> /about", "Headquarters Burlington, North Carolina -> db", "Russ Farmer President/CEO and champion driver/builder -> /", "Custom race car manufacturing (dragsters, roadsters, doorslammers) -> /about, /", "In-house powder coating, polishing, chroming, custom painting and graphics -> /about", "CNC plasma cutting 4''x8'' table cutting aluminum, steel, stainless up to 7 gauge -> /services", "AN hose assembly as authorized Goodridge distributor, sizes -3 to -16 -> /services", "Custom fabrication: aluminum & sheet metal, CAD design, MIG/TIG welding, tube bending -> /services", "Nitrous bottle refills, $20 minimum -> /services", "Materials: aluminum, steel, stainless steel -> /services", "Customers include NHRA Sportsman Nationals winner Anthony Bertozzi and divisional champions at Famoso Raceway, Piedmont, Palm Beach -> /", "Design features: removable crossmember, master cylinder outside driver compartment, optimized driveline angles -> /", "Parts division pricing matches or beats mail-order warehouses -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1988, Race Tech Race Cars and Components has been a leading manufacturer of fine racing machines.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "$20 minimum for nitrous refills", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='race-tech-race-cars-and-components-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Radcliff Wire, Inc. operates from Bristol, Connecticut, in the heart of the Eastern U.S. spring industry. The company was founded over six decades ago to supply spring manufacturers with hard-to-locate flat and shaped wire, and has since grown into a global supplier of custom wire products.

The company produces flat, square, and special shaped wire in more than 60 metals and alloys, managing every step from raw material certification through final delivery. Its in-house capabilities include wire drawing, shaping, and a full suite of testing equipment such as Rockwell hardness testers, tensile testers, laser micrometers, optical comparators, and metallurgical microscopy.

Radcliff Wire serves aerospace, electronics, medical, automotive, and consumer product industries, providing wire that meets exacting standards for each sector. The company also supplies DFARS-compliant material for defense applications and maintains REACH and RoHS compliance for European markets.

Quality differentiation comes from an ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system, a workforce averaging 15 years of wire-industry experience, and a structured cross-training program that ensures consistent competence across all positions.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','REACH compliance','RoHS compliance','Conflict Minerals compliance','DFARS compliance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom shaped wire manufacturing", "Flat wire production", "Square wire production", "Special shaped wire production", "Wire drawing", "Raw material certification", "In-house hardness testing (Rockwell, Knoop/Vickers)", "Tensile testing", "Microscopy (up to 40x)", "Laser micrometry", "Optical comparison", "Metallurgical mounting and digital video imaging", "DFARS compliant material sourcing", "REACH compliance", "RoHS compliance", "Conflict minerals compliance"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Electronics", "Medical", "Automotive", "Consumer products"], "materials": ["Aluminum Alloy", "Brass", "Copper Metal", "Copper Beryllium", "Hastelloy", "Inconel", "Nickel", "Stainless Steel", "Steel", "Tin", "Tin Zinc"], "equipment": ["3 standard Rockwell hardness testers", "3 tensile testers", "1 Knoop/Vickers micro-hardness tester", "1 Ames portable Rockwell hardness tester", "5 microscopes with magnification up to 40x", "2 laser micrometers", "2 optical comparators", "Metallurgical mounting and measuring with Digital Video Image Generator (up to 385x)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "Average employee tenure of 15 years in wire manufacturing", "Rigorous cross-training program for all positions", "DFARS-compliant material sourcing for defense contracts", "In-house metallurgical testing including hardness, tensile, and microscopy"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Bristol, Connecticut -> /about", "Founded over six decades ago -> /about", "Produces flat, square, and special shaped wire in over 60 metals and alloys -> /about", "Serves aerospace, electronics, medical, automotive, consumer products -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "Average employee 15 years experience -> /quality", "Cross-training program for all positions -> /quality", "DFARS compliant material sourcing -> /quality", "REACH compliance -> /quality", "RoHS compliance -> /quality", "Conflict Minerals compliance -> /quality", "Testing equipment: Rockwell hardness testers, tensile testers, Knoop/Vickers micro-hardness tester, Ames portable Rockwell hardness tester, microscopes, laser micrometers, optical comparators, metallurgical mounting -> /quality", "Materials: Aluminum Alloy, Brass, Copper Metal, Copper Beryllium, Hastelloy, Inconel, Nickel, Stainless Steel, Steel, Tin, Tin Zinc -> /quality", "Manufacturer of custom shaped wire -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Radcliff Wire, Inc. produces flat, square, and special shaped wire in over 60 different metals and alloys.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["DFARS compliant"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='radcliff-wire-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Radian Machining has operated from Santa Clara, California since its founding in 1996. The company functions as a contract machining shop, providing CNC milling and turning services to a range of business customers.

The shop specializes in prototype and short-run production parts, leveraging CNC milling and turning processes to deliver machined components. With a workforce of 10 to 49 employees, the facility handles projects from initial prototype development through limited production runs. Its product output includes CNC machined components and prototypes tailored to customer specifications.

Radian Machining serves three primary industry sectors: technology, industrial, and medical. The company''s customer base consists of businesses requiring precision machined parts in low to moderate volumes.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC milling", "CNC turning", "Prototype machining", "Short-run production", "CNC machined components"], "industries": ["Technology", "Industrial", "Medical"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype and short-run production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Specializes in prototype and short-run production", "CNC milling and turning services", "Serves technology, industrial, and medical industries"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 -> db", "Headquartered in Santa Clara, California -> db", "Employee count 10-49 -> db", "Provides CNC milling and turning services -> db", "Specializes in prototype and short-run production parts -> db", "Serves technology, industrial, and medical industries -> db", "Products include CNC machined components and prototypes -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Radian Machining provides CNC milling and turning services, specializing in prototype and short-run production parts.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "10-49", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='radian-machining' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1999 in Huntsville, Alabama, by George Clark, John Dennis, and Scott Dublin, Radiance Technologies began as an employee-owned subcontractor supporting the U.S. Army Space and Missile Defense Command. The company later relocated its corporate headquarters to Ruston, Louisiana.

Radiance delivers intelligence analysis, cyber operations, directed energy systems, hypersonics, space solutions, and AI/ML applications for defense and intelligence customers. Its capabilities span systems engineering, modeling and simulation, software development, prototyping, low-rate manufacturing, and hardware-in-the-loop testing. The firm operates facilities in nine states and project offices in fourteen states, employing over 500 people as of 2015 with revenue of $116.7 million that year.

Primary customers include the U.S. Department of Defense, the Intelligence Community, the U.S. Army (SMDC, INSCOM), NASA, and commercial aerospace firms. The company has supported Army hypersonic missile programs, high-energy laser development, and space-based communication and ISR missions.

The founders structured Radiance as an employee-owned enterprise to align incentives with mission success, emphasizing a culture that tackles problems others deem impossible. Leadership states that this ownership model keeps the focus on delivering game-changing solutions rather than maximizing short-term profit.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Intelligence Analysis", "Cyber Operations", "Directed Energy Systems Engineering", "Hypersonics Development", "Space Systems Engineering", "Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning", "Modeling and Simulation", "Software Development", "Systems Engineering & Integration", "Prototyping & Low-Rate Production", "Hardware-in-the-Loop Testing", "Sensor Design & Integration", "Foreign Materiel Exploitation", "Software Reverse Engineering", "Vulnerability Assessments", "Exploit Development", "Embedded Systems Development", "Real-Time Algorithm Processing", "Aviation System Logistics", "Program Management", "Acquisition Life Cycle Support", "RDT&E Support", "Manufacturing (Hybrid Power Systems)", "Training Systems Development"], "industries": ["Department of Defense", "Intelligence Community", "U.S. Army", "NASA", "Commercial Aerospace"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned structure aligns incentives with customer mission success", "Prioritizes partnering to enhance customer mission over company bottom line", "Culture focused on solving problems others call impossible", "Trusted employee-owners empowered to do the ''right thing''", "Singular focus on game-changing solutions for toughest challenges"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1999 in Huntsville, Alabama by George Clark, John Dennis, Scott Dublin -> /about-us", "Employee-owned -> /about-us and /", "Headquarters Ruston, Louisiana -> db", "500+ employees as of 2015 -> /about-us", "Revenue $116.7M in 2015 -> /about-us", "Facilities in nine states, project offices in fourteen states -> /about-us", "Certifications ISO 9001:2015 and AS9100D -> /quality", "Capabilities list -> /capabilities", "Services list -> /services", "Industries served: DoD, Intelligence Community, Army, NASA -> / and /about-us", "Customer examples: U.S. Army SMDC, INSCOM, NASA -> / and /about-us", "Founders'' goal: employee-owned, team environment, technology focus, operational relevance -> /about-us", "Employee-ownership benefits to customers and workforce -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Capabilities include Manufacturing, Low Rate Initial Production, Prototype Design & Development, and Microelectronics Product Division.", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='radiance-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Raeed & Sons opened its doors in May 2013 at 1105 South 12th Street in Bismarck, North Dakota. The shop is family‑owned and operated by Raeed Douri, who brought over thirty years of electronics experience to the venture. He started the business with a simple mission: give every broken device a fair shot and treat every customer like family.

The shop provides component‑level repair for a wide range of electronics. Services include screen, battery, and charge‑port replacement on smartphones and tablets; hardware upgrades, custom builds, virus removal, and full diagnostics on Windows and Mac computers; and board‑level work on engine control units, transmission modules, power supplies, and industrial PCBs — covering capacitor replacement, IC reflow, and trace repair. Free diagnostics are standard, and most repairs are completed in under an hour. The operation runs as a walk‑in service center with no appointment needed.

Customers span individual consumers with damaged phones or laptops, automotive shops needing ECU or module repair, and industrial clients with faulty control boards or power supplies. The shop’s expertise in component‑level fixes often saves customers the cost of full unit replacement, a value highlighted by automotive and industrial referrals.

