UPDATE companies SET description='Remcon Plastics was founded in November 1982 by Peter and Doren Connors in Pennsylvania. The venture was backed by the Remmey and Connors families — Doren''s parents Bill and Nancy Remmey and Pete''s mother Lorraine Connors — whose savings and names (Remcon = Remmey + Connors) launched the business. The founders believed a small, family-owned rotational molder could compete with larger firms by building more durable products and standing behind them. In 1990, after eight years in Conshohocken, the operation moved to Reading, Pennsylvania, tripling plant size.

Today, Remcon runs a 75,000-square-foot facility in Reading with eight rotational molding machines. It produces material handling containers, MASH-compliant water-filled traffic barricades and longitudinal channelizers, and custom OEM rotationally molded components. Automation and advanced production systems increase capacity and consistency, and the company also works with production partners who share its engineering and quality standards.

Remcon serves traffic safety, material handling, and custom OEM markets. Its traffic safety line includes the Guardsafe 36 barricade and other MASH-compliant channelizers used on jobsites nationwide. One original OEM customer from the early 1980s remains a partner today.

The company''s differentiation traces to its founding principles: durability over shortcuts, thoughtful design to prevent field failures, and integrity in every decision. Pete Connors, still active as president, engineered the "R" lip and replaceable pallet system that extended bin life from months to over a decade, reshaping industry expectations. Leadership has transitioned to the next generation — Tracy Connors as CEO and James Connors as Director of Design — while maintaining the family-owned structure and the original commitment to standing behind every product shipped.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rotational molding", "Custom OEM rotational molding", "Material handling container manufacturing", "MASH-compliant traffic safety product manufacturing", "Water-filled barricade production", "Longitudinal channelizer production", "Automation for rotational molding", "Advanced production systems", "Design and engineering", "Production partner network", "Stress crack resistant polyethylene processing"], "industries": ["Traffic safety", "Material handling", "Custom OEM rotational molding"], "materials": ["Polyethylene", "Stress crack resistant polyethylene (DuPont formulations)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 by Peter and Doren Connors in Pennsylvania -> /about-us", "Family-owned, named after Remmey and Connors families -> /about-us", "Initial investors: Bill and Nancy Remmey, Lorraine Connors -> /about-us", "Moved to Reading, PA in 1990, tripling plant size -> /about-us", "75,000 sq ft facility with 8 rotational molding machines -> /about-us", "Produces material handling containers, MASH-compliant traffic safety products, custom OEM rotationally molded components -> /about-us", "Automation and advanced production systems for capacity -> /about-us", "Works with production partners -> /about-us", "Pete Connors invented \"R\" lip reinforced beaded rim and replaceable pallet system -> /about-us", "Guardsafe 36 barricade introduced 2016 -> /about-us", "MASH-compliant water-filled traffic barricades and longitudinal channelizers -> /about-us", "Material handling products: FBP bin, Dry Bulk Hopper, bulk containers -> /about-us", "Multi-generational leadership: Pete Connors (President), Tracy Connors (EVP/CEO), James Connors (Director of Design) -> /about-us", "One OEM customer from early 1980s still a customer -> /about-us", "Founded on principles: durability, thoughtful design, integrity -> /about-us", "Headquarters: Reading, Pennsylvania -> db", "Founded year: 1982 -> db", "Description includes Family Owned, Rotomolded in USA, Traffic Safety, Material Handling, Custom OEM Solutions -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, the 75,000 square foot facility operates eight rotational molding machines and produces: Material handling containers, MASH-compliant traffic safety products, Custom OEM rotationally molded components", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='remcon-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rencher Industries operates from Winston-Salem, North Carolina, where it focuses on boutique manufacturing for the camera department. The company does not disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or founders'' names in the available materials.

