UPDATE companies SET description='Resonant Link Medical was founded in 2017 in Burlington, Vermont, by Aaron Stein, who serves as chief technology officer. The company emerged from Stein''s postdoctoral research at Dartmouth College, where he pioneered advances in resonant coils and power electronics that enabled new levels of efficiency and range for wireless power transfer.

The company develops the Aurion WPT™ wireless power and data platform, which uses inductive coupling to recharge or continuously power implantable medical devices through the skin without transcutaneous leads. Its product platforms include Eterni™ for millimeter-scale implants (up to 500 mW continuous power), Vivigo™ Fast Charger (20-minute recharge over a large range), and Cardessa™ High Power Platform (10–15 W driveline-free power). Resonant Link also provides feasibility studies and regulatory-ready testing and integration services. To date, the team has designed wireless power solutions for more than 50 implantable device types.

Customers span neuromodulation, cardiac rhythm management, sensing and diagnostics, circulatory assist, cranial and brain-computer interfaces, sleep apnea, implantable drug delivery, urinary and gastrointestinal, and smart orthopedics. Partners include Paradromics, which used the technology to maintain power through thick tissue layers for a brain-computer interface, and Resonetics, which collaborated on next-generation bioelectronic devices. One brain-computer interface company reached human studies within 15 months of development start.

Resonant Link says its mission is to enable smaller, smarter, and longer-lasting implants that help people get well and stay well. The company emphasizes that its platform delivers 10× faster charging than conventional wireless at double the range, allows implants as small as 3 mm, and maintains uninterrupted power and data transfer during patient movement—all while reducing development risk through regulatory-ready processes.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Inductive wireless power transfer", "Wireless data transfer", "Feasibility studies", "Regulatory-ready processes and testing", "Traceable design integration", "High-frequency magnetics design", "Power electronics design", "Thermal management", "Electromagnetic simulation and modeling", "RF systems engineering", "Implantable device platform development (Eterni\u2122, Vivigo\u2122, Cardessa\u2122)"], "industries": ["Neuromodulation", "Cardiac Rhythm Management", "Sensing & Diagnostics", "Circulatory Assist", "Cranial & Brain-Computer Interfaces", "Sleep Apnea", "Implantable Drug Delivery", "Urinary & GI", "Smart Orthopedics"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["10\u00d7 faster wireless charging than conventional methods at double the range", "20-minute recharge capability for implantable devices", "Implants as small as 3 mm enabled by Eterni\u2122 platform", "Uninterrupted power and data transfer during patient movement", "Regulatory-ready processes that helped a BCI company reach human studies in 15 months"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2017 by Aaron Stein -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Burlington, Vermont -> db", "Aurion WPT\u2122 wireless power and data platform -> /", "Product platforms: Eterni\u2122, Vivigo\u2122, Cardessa\u2122 -> /", "50+ implantable device types designed -> /", "10x faster charging over double range -> /", "20-minute wireless charging -> /", "Implants as small as 3 mm -> /", "Uninterrupted power/dat