UPDATE companies SET description='Restoration & Performance Motorcars operates from a red barn on Monkton Road in Vergennes, Vermont. The business traces its roots to 1986 when Peter Markowski, a Vermont native who had spent two decades restoring a Ferrari Barchetta to its original specification, built the shop to turn his passion for classic European sports cars into a full-time venture. Markowski, the oldest of eight children from a dairy farm, had previously worked in construction, banking, and heavy-truck sales before founding the company.

