 -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Steel and Miscellaneous Metal Fabrication", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='robco-steel-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Roberto''s Sofa Factory operates from Phoenix, Arizona, where it has served the Arizona Valley for decades. The business began in a garage when Roberto, an immigrant from Mexico, founded a small family-owned upholstery shop driven by a passion for craftsmanship. Today, the company remains family-owned and operated, with Roberto''s sons, brother, and grandchildren working alongside each other in the shop.

The shop provides a full range of upholstery services, including custom cushion design and creation, sofa and couch reupholstery, chair and recliner upholstery, sectional reupholstery, frame repair and reinforcement, spring replacement, leather upholstery and repair, mid-century modern and antique furniture restoration, pattern matching, foam cutting and replacement, stitching and seam repair, zipper repair, and decorative trims such as piping, tufting, and nailheads. The team also handles commercial projects for hotels, restaurants, and offices, and offers weather‑resistant fabrics for outdoor furniture. Work follows a four‑step process: consultation and design planning, furniture preparation, upholstery and detailing, and final inspection with delivery or pickup.

Clients range from residential homeowners seeking to restore a favorite piece to businesses in the hospitality and corporate sectors needing contract‑grade upholstery. The company serves all of Arizona, with recent projects spanning private homes, restaurants, offices, and hotels.

Roberto''s Sofa Factory distinguishes itself by educating customers at every stage, emphasizing transparency about timelines, costs, and materials. The family legacy centers on treating each piece as if it were their own and each customer like family, a philosophy that has generated word‑of‑mouth referrals and repeat business over decades.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cushion design and creation", "Sofa and couch reupholstery", "Chair and recliner upholstery", "Sectional reupholstery", "Frame repair and reinforcement", "Spring replacement and adjustment", "Leather upholstery and repair", "Mid-century modern furniture reupholstery", "Antique furniture restoration", "Pattern matching for fabric designs", "Foam cutting and replacement", "Cushion refilling and replacement", "Stitching and seam repair", "Zipper repair", "Decorative trims, nailheads, and finishes", "Hotel furniture upholstery", "Commercial upholstery for restaurants and offices", "Outdoor furniture upholstery with weather-resistant fabrics", "Consultation and design planning", "Furniture preparation and inspection", "Upholstery and detailing", "Final inspection and delivery"], "industries": ["Residential", "Hospitality", "Commercial offices", "Restaurants", "Hotels"], "materials": ["Fabric", "Leather", "Foam", "Weather-resistant fabric", "Decorative trims", "Nailheads"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Educates clients about every step of the upholstery process", "Family\u2011operated with pride, honesty, and attention to detail", "Treats every piece like its own and every customer like family", "Four\u2011step process from consultation through final inspection", "Offers weather\u2011resistant fabrics for outdoor furniture"], "facts_used": ["Location: Phoenix, Arizona -> /", "Family-owned, founded by Roberto from Mexico -> /about-us", "Services list -> /", "Process steps -> /", "Industries served: residential, commercial, hospitality -> /", "Differentiators: education, family values, transparency -> /", "Materials: fabric, leather, foam, weather-resistant fabrics, decorative trims, nailheads -> /", "Headquarters address: 3410 W Flower St, Phoenix, AZ 85017 -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Cushion Design and Creation, Sofa and Couch Reupholstery, Chair and Recliner Upholstery, Sectional Reupholstery, Frame Repair and Reinforcement, Spring Replacement and Adjustment, Leather Upholstery and Repair, Mid-Century Modern Furniture Reupholstery, Antique Furniture Restoration", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='roberto-s-sofa-factory' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Robling Medical, LLC operates from Youngsville, North Carolina, where it has accumulated over 35 years of medical device manufacturing experience. The company focuses exclusively on medical devices, with more than 75 percent of its work in interventional and minimally invasive surgical applications.

As a full-service contract manufacturer, Robling handles design for manufacturing and assembly, prototyping, and benchtop performance characterization, with early emphasis on material, tooling, and process selection. Its capabilities span sterile disposable manufacturing — including bonding, tipping, heat sealing, ultrasonic welding, and kitting — as well as electro-mechanical assembly, box builds, cable and harness assembly, PC board flashing, and functional testing. The firm also provides vertically integrated packaging services, running high-speed Multivac lines with inline printing on Tyvek 1073B, paper, and poly film, and manages contract sterilization via ethylene oxide, gamma, and electron beam. Annual output exceeds 10 million sterile devices, from prototype runs to full-scale production.

Robling serves medical device and life sciences OEMs across a broad range of clinical markets: women’s health, urology, fluid management, cardiology, orthopedics, neurology, oncology, gastrointestinal, ENT, vascular, and respiratory. Customers include large, mid-sized, and newly commercialized MedTech original equipment manufacturers.

The company differentiates itself through cross-market experience that it says yields proven processes, faster ramp-up, and fewer surprises. Its quality system is described as flexible and collaborative, offering clients the option to use Robling’s QMS or work within their own. Quality certifications include MDD 93/42/EEC, Japan PMDA Foreign Manufacturer Accreditation, Brazil ANVISA certification, compliance with SOR/92-282, and Korean GMP compliance.', certifications=ARRAY['MDD 93/42/EEC','Japan PMDA Foreign Manufacturer Accreditation #BG3040155','Brazil ANVISA Certified','Compliant with SOR/92-282','Korean GMP Compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DFM/DFA)", "Prototyping", "Benchtop performance characterization", "Material, tooling, and manufacturing process selection", "Full-service project management of V&V testing", "In-house assembly", "Sterilization validation", "Packaging validation", "Bonding", "Tipping", "Heat sealing", "Ultrasonic welding", "Kitting", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "Box builds", "Cable and harness assembly", "PC board flashing", "PC imaging", "Functional testing", "Form, fill, and seal (flexible and rigid medical packaging)", "Regulatory labeling", "Contract sterilization services (EtO, Gamma, E-Beam)", "High-speed Multivac lines with inline printing (Tyvek 1073B, paper, poly film)", "Regulatory support (V&V protocols, clinical studies, sterilization and biocompatibility protocols)", "Quality system collaboration (flexible QMS)"], "industries": ["Medical device", "Life sciences", "Women''s health", "Urology", "Fluid management", "Cardiology", "Orthopedics", "Neurology", "Oncology", "Gastrointestinal", "ENT", "Vascular", "Respiratory", "Interventional", "Minimally invasive surgery (MIS)"], "materials": ["Tyvek 1073B", "Paper", "Poly Film"], "equipment": ["High-speed Multivac\u2122 lines with inline printing"], "volume": "Prototype to full-scale production; >10 million sterile devices annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Cross-market experience for faster ramp-up and fewer surprises", "Flexible QMS: use Robling\u2019s system or integrate with customer\u2019s", "Full-service V&V project management with in-house assembly, sterilization, and packaging validation", "Vertically integrated packaging with high-speed Multivac lines and inline printing", "Contract sterilization management for EtO, Gamma, and E-Beam"], "facts_used": ["Location: Youngsville, North Carolina -> db", "35+ years of medical device experience -> /", "100% medical device focus -> /", ">75% interventional + MIS -> /", ">10,000,000 sterile devices produced annually -> /", "Design for Manufacturing and Assembly, prototyping, benchtop performance characterization -> /", "Full-service project management of V&V testing, in-house assembly, sterilization and packaging validations -> /", "Experts in bonding, tipping, heat sealing, ultrasonic welding, kitting -> /", "Electro-mechanical assembly, box builds, cable/harness assembly, PC board flashing, PC imaging, functional test -> /", "Form, fill, seal for flexible and rigid medical packaging with regulatory labeling -> /", "Contract sterilization services (EtO, Gamma, E-Beam) -> /", "High-speed Multivac lines with inline printing (Tyvek 1073B, paper, poly film) -> /", "Clinical markets: women''s health, urology, fluid management, cardiology, orthopedics, neurology, oncology, gastrointestinal, ENT, vascular, respiratory -> /", "Quality certifications: MDD 93/42/EEC, Japan PMDA Foreign Manufacturer Accreditation #BG3040155, Brazil ANVISA Certified, Compliant with SOR/92-282, Korean GMP Compliant -> /quality", "Flexible QMS approach -> /quality", "Cross-market experience means proven processes, faster ramp-up, fewer surprises -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Robling Medical | Full Service Contract Manufacturer", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cag