UPDATE companies SET description='Rockland Foodservice operates from a store in Rockland, Maine. The business has existed in one form or another since the 1980s, originally as Rockland Wholesale in a building now occupied by J.Edward Knight Insurance, and later next door where CarQuest Auto Parts stands. It is part of a family-owned group that also included Shore Save, a former grocery located where a Rite Aid now stands, and the company has served the Rockland community for decades.

The company functions as a foodservice distributor and retailer, stocking a wide variety of food and beverage items for immediate pickup or curbside collection. It taps into a network of local and out-of-state distributors to source specialty products, typically fulfilling such requests within a few days. The facility also handles bulk and big-pack orders for events such as weddings, parties, and boat trips, with customers able to place orders a week in advance for staged pickup.

Primary customers include local restaurants, hotels, and individual consumers planning large gatherings. The business positions itself between national broadline distributors and conventional retail chains, aiming to serve both commercial foodservice operators and retail shoppers in the mid-coast Maine region.

Rockland Foodservice was founded to fill the gap between large food distributors and retail chains, with a stated mission to "Feed Maine" through exemplary service and competitive prices. The emphasis on personal attention—bending over backwards for each customer, whether new or lifelong—reflects its community-rooted approach.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["In-store shopping", "Curbside pickup", "Bulk order fulfillment", "Specialty item sourcing", "Foodservice distribution"], "industries": ["Foodservice distribution", "Restaurant supply", "Hospitality", "Event catering", "Retail food"], "materials": ["Foodservice products", "Beverages", "Bulk food items"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "A few days for specialty items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fills the gap between large food distributors and retail chains", "Exemplary service and competitive prices", "Curbside pickup available", "Specialty items sourced within a few days", "Bulk and big-pack orders for events with advance staging"], "facts_used": ["Located at 195 Park Street, Rockland, Maine -> /", "In business since the 1980s, previously Rockland Wholesale -> /", "Family-owned, part of Shore Save group -> /", "Serves local restaurants, hotels, and individuals -> /", "Offers curbside service and bulk orders for events -> /", "Sources specialty items from local and out-of-state distributors within a few days -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We fill the gap between the big food distributors and the retail chains you are used to.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rockland-foodservice' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rockledge Farm Woodworks operates from a 200-year-old hill farm in Reading, Vermont, where a family-owned woodworking tradition spans four generations. The business traces its roots to a mail-order venture that sold wooden furniture from the farm, and today the converted barns house workshops, a gallery, and offices for the small, family-operated company.

The workshop produces custom furniture and one-of-a-kind pieces crafted from sustainably harvested Vermont hardwoods such as birdseye maple, curly maple, black walnut, cherry, flame birch, and various burls. Each project begins with hand-selected lumber sourced from small local mills, and the team builds everything from heirloom tables and chairs to accessories including cutting boards, bowls, utensils, jewelry boxes, game boards, and bentwood oval ware. No two pieces are identical; the firm describes its output as “one-of-a-kind, one-at-a-time” handcrafted work.

Customers include private clients who collaborate on custom designs as well as select galleries and stores across the country that carry the accessory line. The company does not operate as a production shop with a fixed catalog; instead, it treats every commission as a fresh start, developing designs directly with the buyer.

The founders’ philosophy centers on letting the wood itself guide the design—unusual live-edge slabs may sit for years until the “proper use becomes apparent”—and on keeping the supply chain local unless a specific material cannot be found in Vermont. This approach, they say, distinguishes them from volume-oriented furniture makers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and fabrication", "Live edge / figured wood furniture", "Handcrafted wood accessories (cutting boards, bowls, utensils, jewelry boxes, game boards, bentwood oval ware)", "Wood selection and sourcing from local mills", "Sustainable harvesting practices", "Gallery retail and direct sales"], "industries": ["Custom furniture", "Artisan wood accessories", "Gallery retail"], "materials": ["Birdseye Maple", "Curly Maple", "Black Walnut", "Cherry", "Oak", "Flame Birch", "Burls", "Vermont native hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One-of-a-kind, one-at-a-time handcrafted heirlooms", "Sustainably harvested Vermont native hardwoods hand-selected from local mills", "Custom design collaboration on each project", "Four-generation woodworking heritage on a 200-year-old hill farm", "Converted historic barns as workshops and gallery"], "facts_used": ["Family-owned, small Vermont farm in Reading, Vermont -> /", "Four generations of woodworking heritage, previously mail order business -> /about", "Located on 200-year-old hill farm with converted barns for workshops, gallery, office -> /about", "Makes custom furniture and one-of-a-kind pieces from live edge/figured woods -> /about", "Produces accessories: cutting/serving boards, bowls, utensils, jewelry boxes, game boards/tables, bentwood oval ware -> /about", "Uses sustainably harvested local Vermont woods: Birdseye Maple, Curly Maple, Black Walnut, Cherry, Flame Birch, Burls -> /", "Wood hand-selected from small local lumber mills -> /about", "Each piece is one-of-a-kind, one-at-a-time, handcrafted heirloom -> /about", "Sells through select galleries and stores around the nation -> /about", "Antithesis of production shop, custom design collaboration with clients -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a small, family owned Vermont farm which has been crafting exquisite custom furniture from the finest native wood for generations.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rockledge-farm-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rockport Steel operates in Rockport, Maine, on the state''s Midcoast. The shop has been producing custom metal fabrications for over 30 years, beginning with a small crew building boats before expanding into structural steel and architectural metalwork.

The company provides forming, welding, cutting, design consulting, shop drawings with 3D modeling, and installation services. Its capabilities cover structural steel fabrication, custom architectural metalwork, railings, stairs, fences, gates, boat components, docks, ramps, commercial signage, and sculptures. A boom truck supports on-site erection.

Rockport Steel serves both commercial and residential clients. Project examples include structural frameworks for buildings, ornamental railings and staircases, perimeter fencing and gates, marine fabrications for boats and docks, custom signs, and artistic sculptures. The firm emphasizes a collaborative approach, working from customer concepts through to finished installation.

The company states its goal is to deliver superior quality and workmanship that exceeds expectations, with a diverse team that brings strong problem-solving skills to each custom design. It positions itself as a resource partner, telling clients: "You provide the vision, we provide the resources."', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal forming", "Welding", "Metal cutting", "Design consulting", "Shop drawings and 3D modeling", "Installation", "Structural steel fabrication", "Architectural metal fabrication", "Boom truck operation"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Residential construction", "Marine", "Signage", "Art and sculpture"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Boom truck"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom design and fabrication from concept to installation", "In-house shop drawings and 3D modeling", "Boom truck for on-site installation", "Over 30 years of metal fabrication experience", "Diverse team with strong problem-solving skills"], "facts_used": ["Location: Rockport, Maine -> /about-us", "Founded narrative: started with a couple of employees building boats -> /about-us", "Services: forming, welding, cutting, consulting, drawings, installation -> /", "Industries: commercial and residential -> /about-us", "Equipment: boom truck -> /", "Capabilities: structural steel fabrication, architectural metal fabrication -> /about-us", "Differentiators: superior quality and workmanship, custom design -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializes in custom metal fabrication projects both commercial and residential", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rockport-steel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rogue Welding & Fabrication operates from Gardiner, Maine, off Route 201. The company is owned by Devon Sproul, who brings nearly a decade of professional fabrication experience spanning corporate industrial welding and small‑business metal repair.

The shop provides stick (SMAW), MIG (GMAW), and AC/DC TIG (GTAW) welding, along with CNC plasma cutting on a table added in 2024. Work covers aluminum, stainless steel, and carbon steel, ranging from small repairs to full custom fabrication. A portable engine‑driven rig enables on‑site repairs throughout Maine, while the Gardiner facility handles projects of all sizes.

Customers include owners of fishing vessels, work trailers, tow trucks, and snowmobile trailers, as well as residential clients seeking custom signs, fire pits, and home‑garage items. The company also takes on industrial component work and offers on‑site planning consultations for larger projects.

