UPDATE companies SET description='SEC America Corp operates from South Burlington, Vermont, where it has developed power conversion solutions for more than three decades. The company was founded as a design and engineering firm specializing in the supply of electricity, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The company designs, engineers, and assembles rugged power conversion products in the United States. Its portfolio includes DC-DC converters, battery backups, sealed converters, and trailer electrical interfaces that resolve electrical mismatches between tractors and trailers. SEC America maintains engineering facilities for rapid prototype development and field test monitoring, along with in-house transformer and metal fabrication capabilities that support design management and product refinement. An extensive inventory of standard off-the-shelf units is warehoused at the South Burlington location, enabling same-day shipment for orders placed before 1:00 PM Eastern time. Custom design and private labeling services are also offered, with the engineering staff tailoring mechanical and electrical specifications to customer requirements.

SEC America serves industrial and consumer specialty markets, with a focus on original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) that require power conversion solutions. Its trailer electrical interfaces target the heavy-duty transportation sector, while its broader product line addresses diverse industrial and consumer applications. The company emphasizes a design/build process that adapts existing designs for small and medium runs and pursues custom development for large-volume programs.

The company differentiates itself through U.S. assembly, rapid delivery on new designs, and a commitment to rugged, built-to-last products. Continuous communication with manufacturing partners is cited as a driver of cost-effective assemblies and packaging. A two-year limited warranty covers defects in materials and workmanship, and warranty and non-warranty repair services are handled at the Vermont facility.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Power conversion design and engineering", "Rapid prototype development", "Field test monitoring", "Custom mechanical and electrical design", "Private labeling", "Transformer fabrication", "Metal fabrication", "U.S. assembly", "Warehousing and same-day shipping", "Warranty repair (2-year limited warranty)", "Off-the-shelf product selection", "Design/build process for OEMs"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Consumer specialty", "OEM", "Transportation"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping for in-stock orders placed before 1:00 PM EST", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on stocked orders placed before 1:00 PM EST", "Products assembled in the USA", "Rapid prototype development with field test monitoring", "Custom design and private labeling services", "In-house transformer and metal fabrication facilities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in South Burlington, Vermont -> db", "More than 30 years track record -> /about", "Design and engineering company specializing in power conversion solutions -> /about", "Engineering facilities for rapid prototype development and field test monitoring -> /about", "Custom design and private labeling services -> /about", "Transformer and metal fabrication facilities -> /about", "Products assembled in the USA -> /about", "Extensive inventory warehoused in South Burlington, Vermont -> /about", "Same-day shipping for orders placed before 1:00 PM -> /about", "Products: DC-DC converters, battery backups, sealed converters